Lumen OS: SBC at 48 kHz for the A2DP source (Play 6 base only).

The XGIMI Play 6 audio HAL (audio.primary.mt5889) plays A2DP itself: a loopback copies its 48 kHz DSP output
into the Bluetooth stream without resampling. AOSP offers SBC at 44.1 kHz only, so a Bluetooth speaker played
everything about 8 % slow and low (owner 2026-10-24, Yandex Station). Stock XGIMI firmware ran SBC at 48 kHz.
Source caps get 48 kHz (a mandatory SBC sink rate) and the default config prefers it; peers without 48 kHz
still get 44.1 kHz.

diff -ruN a/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc.cc b/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc.cc
--- a/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc.cc	2026-10-24 13:14:07.668560897 +0300
+++ b/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc.cc	2026-10-24 13:14:07.695630538 +0300
@@ -56,7 +56,9 @@
 
 /* SBC Source codec capabilities */
 static const tA2DP_SBC_CIE a2dp_sbc_source_caps = {
-    (A2DP_SBC_IE_SAMP_FREQ_44),                         /* samp_freq */
+    // Lumen OS (Play 6): 48 kHz too. The mt5889 audio HAL feeds the A2DP stream from its 48 kHz DSP without
+    // resampling; at 44.1 kHz a Bluetooth speaker played it slow and low. Every SBC sink supports 48 kHz.
+    (A2DP_SBC_IE_SAMP_FREQ_48 | A2DP_SBC_IE_SAMP_FREQ_44), /* samp_freq */
     (A2DP_SBC_IE_CH_MD_MONO | A2DP_SBC_IE_CH_MD_JOINT), /* ch_mode */
     (A2DP_SBC_IE_BLOCKS_16 | A2DP_SBC_IE_BLOCKS_12 | A2DP_SBC_IE_BLOCKS_8 |
      A2DP_SBC_IE_BLOCKS_4),            /* block_len */
@@ -83,7 +85,7 @@
 
 /* Default SBC codec configuration */
 const tA2DP_SBC_CIE a2dp_sbc_default_config = {
-    A2DP_SBC_IE_SAMP_FREQ_44,          /* samp_freq */
+    A2DP_SBC_IE_SAMP_FREQ_48,          /* samp_freq: Lumen OS (Play 6), 48 kHz first (see the source caps) */
     A2DP_SBC_IE_CH_MD_JOINT,           /* ch_mode */
     A2DP_SBC_IE_BLOCKS_16,             /* block_len */
     A2DP_SBC_IE_SUBBAND_8,             /* num_subbands */
